## 18. Final Design Direction

I want Plotline to feel like opening a beautifully designed writer's notebook.

The experience should be feminine, thoughtful, visually delightful, and inspiring.

The central idea is:

**A writer should be able to explore an entirely different version of their story without losing the version they already love.**

Every major design decision should support that principle.

Make the pink theme feel memorable and premium. Use gorgeous typography, blush and strawberry tones, elegant cards, subtle animations, and excellent information hierarchy.

This is a project I eventually want to feature in my UX and AI product design portfolio, so the design should feel professional and distinctive.

However, functionality matters more than visual decoration.

Start by implementing a working application with the essential project management, character bible, canon protection, and Gemini-powered What-If Engine.

Once those features are functioning, continue expanding the application without breaking existing functionality.

**Build the actual interactive application now, with working data persistence and real AI generation.**